      "status": "PRESENT",
      "chunk_id": "text_0",
      "quote": "Association between adherence to the Mediterranean diet and metabolic syndrome in children and adolescents: a systematic review and meta-­ analysis.",
      "reason": "The title explicitly includes the phrase 'systematic review', identifying the report as a systematic review."
    },
    {
      "element_id": "prisma_2020_1_e2",
      "status": "PRESENT",
      "chunk_id": "text_0",
      "quote": "Association between adherence to the Mediterranean diet and metabolic syndrome in children and adolescents: a systematic review and meta-­ analysis.",
      "reason": "The title specifies the population ('children and adolescents') and the exposure/outcome focus ('adherence to the Mediterranean diet' and 'metabolic syndrome'), providing key information about the review question."
    },
    {
      "element_id": "prisma_2020_1_e3",
      "status": "PRESENT",
      "chunk_id": "text_0",
      "quote": "Association between adherence to the Mediterranean diet and metabolic syndrome in children and adolescents: a systematic review and meta-­ analysis.",
      "reason": "The title includes 'meta-analysis', which is relevant supplementary information about the analysis method used in the review."
    }
  ],
  "confidence": 90
}

{
  "item_id": "PRISMA_2020_3",
  "elements": [
    {
      "element_id": "prisma_2020_3_e1",
      "status": "PRESENT",
      "chunk_id": "text_3",
      "quote": "Background The Mediterranean diet has been associated with improved metabolic health among adults. This meta-­ analysis aimed to evaluate the association between adherence to a Mediterranean diet and metabolic syndrome among children and adolescents.",
      "reason": "The abstract states the existing knowledge (association in adults) and frames the review aim to evaluate this association in children/adolescents, indicating the current state of knowledge and the uncertainty in younger populations."
    },
    {
      "element_id": "prisma_2020_3_e2",
      "status": "PRESENT",
      "chunk_id": "text_3",
      "quote": "This meta-­ analysis aimed to evaluate the association between adherence to a Mediterranean diet and metabolic syndrome among children and adolescents.",
      "reason": "The manuscript explicitly explains the purpose/need for the review by stating it aims to evaluate the association in children and adolescents, implying the importance of addressing this question in that population."
    },
    {
      "element_id": "prisma_2020_3_e3",
      "status": "MISSING",
      "chunk_id": null,
      "quote": null,
      "reason": "No text in the provided evidence discusses existing systematic reviews, the need for the current review relative to prior reviews, or cites previous reviews."
    },
    {
      "element_id": "prisma_2020_3_e4",
      "status": "NOT_APPLICABLE",
      "chunk_id": null,
      "quote": null,
      "reason": "This review assesses associations between diet adherence and metabolic syndrome (observational), not effects of an intervention; the requirement to describe an intervention mechanism does not apply."
    },
    {
      "element_id": "prisma_2020_3_e5",
      "status": "NOT_APPLICABLE",
      "chunk_id": null,
      "quote": null,
      "reason": "The review does not evaluate a complex intervention or delivery context, so a logic model is not applicable."
    }
  ],
  "confidence": 85
}

{
  "item_id": "PRISMA_2020_4",
  "elements": [
    {
      "element_id": "prisma_2020_4_e1",
      "status": "MISSING",
      "chunk_id": null,
      "quote": null,
      "reason": "No explicit statement of the review objectives or research question is present in the retrieved evidence. The provided chunks describe methods, eligibility criteria, and findings but do not include an explicit objectives or question statement."
    },
    {
      "element_id": "prisma_2020_4_e2",
      "status": "NOT_APPLICABLE",
      "chunk_id": "text_6",
      "quote": "To be eligible for inclusion in the present review, studies needed to meet the following criteria: (i) were children or adolescents aged 5-19 years, all countries and ethnic backgrounds; (ii) had a MetS outcome; (iii) had an adherence to the MedDiet assessed by a validated questionnaire; and (iv) had a longitudinal and cross-­ sectional study design.",
      "reason": "This review examines associations in observational (cross-sectional and longitudinal) studies of adherence to the Mediterranean diet and metabolic syndrome rather than effects of interventions; therefore PICO-style planned comparisons for intervention effects are not applicable."
    }
  ],
  "confidence": 80
}

{
  "item_id": "PRISMA_2020_5",
  "elements": [
    {
      "element_id": "prisma_2020_5_e1",
      "status": "PRESENT",
      "chunk_id": "text_6",
      "quote": "To be eligible for inclusion in the present review, studies needed to meet the following criteria: (i) were children or adolescents aged 5-19 years, all countries and ethnic backgrounds; (ii) had a MetS outcome; (iii) had a adherence to the MedDiet assessed by a validated questionnaire; and (iv) had a longitudinal and cross-­ sectional study design.",
      "reason": "The manuscript specifies key study characteristics used to determine eligibility (age range, population scope, outcome of interest, requirement for validated MedDiet assessment, and eligible study designs)."
    },
    {
      "element_id": "prisma_2020_5_e2",
      "status": "PARTIAL",
      "chunk_id": "text_8",
      "quote": "A search strategy was used to identify all eligible studies published before 22 April 2024.",
      "reason": "The report specifies a search cut-off date (dissemination timing). Language restriction is reported elsewhere ('we restricted our inclusion criteria to studies published in English'), but publication/report status (eg, unpublished data, grey literature) is not described, so the reporting of report characteristics is incomplete."
    },
    {
      "element_id": "prisma_2020_5_e3",
      "status": "MISSING",
      "chunk_id": null,
      "quote": null,
      "reason": "No evidence was provided that the review distinguished excluding studies because outcomes were not measured from excluding studies because outcome results were not reported."
    },
    {
      "element_id": "prisma_2020_5_e4",
      "status": "PRESENT",
      "chunk_id": "text_17",
      "quote": "Children and adolescents with low adherence to the MedDiet had greater odds of developing MetS compared to those with medium to high adherence.",
      "reason": "The syntheses are defined by comparison groups (low adherence vs medium-to-high adherence) linked to the review objective of association between MedDiet adherence and MetS."
    },
    {
      "element_id": "prisma_2020_5_e5",
      "status": "PRESENT",
      "chunk_id": "text_6",
      "quote": "However, to narrow the scope of the meta-­ analysis, only studies that associated the MedDiet with the outcome of MetS were included.",
      "reason": "A rationale for a notable restriction (limiting the meta-analysis to studies that directly associated MedDiet with MetS) is explicitly provided."
    }
  ],
  "confidence": "85"
}

